# Secret Identity, Reveal, takes only "target creature you control": Bot2's Ornithopter is not offered as its target, Bot1's
# is. Bot2 answers with Lightning Bolt on that Ornithopter; it dies, so Secret Identity's only target is illegal when it would
# resolve and it does nothing (CR 608.2b): it goes to the graveyard, and no effect remains on anything.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Ornithopter
Secret Identity
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Ornithopter
Lightning Bolt
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Secret Identity.Cast
Bot1.Modes(Reveal)
! Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Sapphire
Bot1.Graveyard = Secret Identity; Ornithopter
Bot2.Battlefield = Mox Ruby; Ornithopter
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 0
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
